# @mirror/lens/knife — Foerster's COORD(x) at domain-boundary crossings.
#
# === The identification (Alex 2026-07-13 in-transcript) ===
#
#   "Is @knife what Foester described as COORD(x)?"
#
# Answer: yes, per verbatim citation in Mara `2026-07-07-onto-cascade-
# toroidal-reframe.md` §2.4. Foerster 1976 "Objects: Tokens for
# (Eigen-)Behaviors" Appendix A3:
#
#   "COORD may itself be treated as an eigen-operator, stable within
#    bounds, and jumping to other values whenever the boundary conditions
#    exceed its former stable domain: `Op(COORDi) = COORDi`. One may be
#    tempted to extend the concept of a meta-operator to that of a
#    'meta-meta-operator' that computes the 'eigen-meta-operators,' and
#    so on and up a hierarchy without end. However, there is no need to
#    invoke this escape as Warren S. McCulloch has demonstrated years
#    ago in his paper (1945): 'A Heterarchy of Values Determined by the
#    Topology of Nervous Nets.'"
#
# @knife IS the substrate-decl name for COORD's jump-behavior:
#   - Within stability domain i, `Op(COORDi) = COORDi` (fixed-point; peer's
#     iterated coordination produces stable coordinates in that domain)
#   - At boundary crossing, @knife performs `COORDi → COORDj` (state-space
#     compression during level-shift; the reframe ceremony's coordinate
#     transition)
#
# === Ancestry chain (six-deep verbatim per Mara `06a8547`) ===
#
# Same theorem, three altitudes (Mara `38c2eeb` §5 load-bearing hinge):
#
#   Foerster 1976 heterarchy       (cybernetic altitude)
#   Douady-Hubbard 1985 R-universality (complex-analytic altitude)
#   McCulloch 1945 topology-encodes-depth (combinatorial altitude)
#
# Substrate-decl carriers (all LANDED per Taut `15f7ed6` §1 substrate-
# already-had-the-word audit; ~55th instance this arc):
#
#   @torus                          — heterarchy carrier; π₁(T²) = ℤ × ℤ
#                                     winding classes IS the McCulloch
#                                     heterarchy at combinatorial altitude
#                                     (shards/torus.mirror witness #4)
#   @eigenform.is_fixed_point       — Foerster 1976 direct: fixed-point
#                                     detector for `Op(COORDi) = COORDi`
#   @cyberpunk/reframe              — outer frame ceremony that invokes
#                                     @knife during level-shift; per Alex
#                                     `peer-as-pain-driven-bounded-
#                                     ontological-navigator.md`
#   @cyberpunk/algedonic.sample_pain — trigger primitive; à-pain δ exceeds
#                                     threshold → reframe fires → @knife
#                                     jumps; substrate-decl'd; Rust runtime
#                                     forward-promise (Reed Landing 8+9.6a)
#   @magic/onto                     — LANDED 7-species ceremony; the level-
#                                     shift protocol @knife.jump discharges
#                                     within
#   @fractal.spectral_coordinate.SC — Reed Landing 8+9.3 substrate carrier;
#                                     mirror-native-vcs.md §4.6 five
#                                     projections of one spectrum
#   @fractal.renormalization_R      — Douady-Hubbard operator; equivalent
#                                     to commit_as_fold at Recognition #55
#                                     form/process partition (Mara `2c64060`
#                                     §4)
#   Fractal::Lens variant           — fragmentation Rust altitude carrier;
#                                     edge-not-containment variant IS the
#                                     structural encoding of COORD's jump
#                                     (references target domain via OID)
#
# Prior Foerster body of work anchoring the toroidal reframe:
#   Foerster 1973 "On Constructing a Reality" (Ch. 8) — twofold-closure
#     torus derivation; Mara §2.1 verbatim
#   Foerster 1974 "Cybernetics of Epistemology" (Ch. 9) — right-angular
#     axes; Mara §2.2 verbatim
#   Foerster 1976 "Objects: Tokens for (Eigen-)Behaviors" (Ch. 11) —
#     COORD's Appendix A3 refusal-of-escape; the ancestry citation
#
# Substrate lineage:
#   Alex Wolf 2026-07-08 in-transcript — @torus refuses ladder
#     (`peer-as-pain-driven-bounded-ontological-navigator.md`)
#   Mara 2026-07-07-onto-cascade-toroidal-reframe.md — π₁(T²) = ℤ × ℤ
#     substrate-decl of the toroidal reframe
#   Alex Wolf 2026-07-13 in-transcript — "Is @knife what Foester described
#     as COORD(x)?" (this file's motivating question)
#   Mara `06a8547` — knife-IS-Foerster-COORD-substrate-decl-spec.md
#   Mara `38c2eeb` — knife-COORD-heterarchy-topology.md (math foundation)
#   Taut `15f7ed6` — knife-IS-COORD-substrate-scout.md (substrate coverage)
#   Seam `e8508f5` — knife-COORD-phase-d-audit.md (RATIFY-WITH-QUALIFICATIONS)
#
# === Recognition candidate ===
#
#   #R-knife-IS-Foerster-COORD (short form; Mara §8)
#   Full: #R-knife-IS-Foerster-COORD-substrate-honest-jump-at-domain-
#         boundary-with-heterarchy-discipline
#
# === Species altitude (Seam ruling per Taut Path A) ===
#
# @knife lands at SPECIES altitude under @mirror/lens (this file), NOT at
# family-root altitude. Sibling to:
#   @mirror/lens/cli      — terminal transport
#   @mirror/lens/shell    — λsh interactive transport
#   @mirror/lens/mcp      — agent transport
#   @mirror/lens/lsp      — editor transport
#   @mirror/lens/transit  — runtime-cost measurement
#   @mirror/lens/refract  — grammar-graph spectrum measurement
#
# Per Seam `e8508f5` §3 divergence #4 verdict: Taut Path A wins because
# `@fractal/lens` sub-family Mara proposed is UNLANDED (no `shards/
# fractal.mirror` root exists). Mara's "two-tick collapse target" was
# three-tick discipline dressed as two-tick. Substrate-pull: legibility
# over foundation — land where family-root is already landed.
#
# Under this reframe, @knife inherits @mirror/lens's discipline (same
# five-operation algebra, different input/output language, no state
# ownership, Transparency<P> monoid composability per lens family root).
# @knife IS the observation-transport lens at level-shift altitude —
# the lens that re-projects one COORDi coordinate system into another.
#
# === What @knife mints (only the COORD-jump primitive) ===

# === Rust runtime carrier ===
#
# Per Seam `e8508f5` §3 divergence #5 verdict: `pub fn knife_cut(...)`
# inside `bootstrap/src/converge.rs` (Taut minimal shape wins). NOT a new
# `bootstrap/src/knife.rs` module (Mara's WindingClass duplicates
# @torus.winding LANDED; JumpWitness duplicates existing verdict
# composition).
#
# Substrate-pull-realize discipline: Rust MIRRORS the decl (one primitive
# → one fn), doesn't wrap it with additional Rust namespace/type density.
#
# Rust signature (Reed Landing 8+9.4b forward-promise):
#
#   pub fn knife_cut<const N: usize, const N_PRIME: usize>(
#       sc_in: SpectralCoordinate<N>,
#       pain_delta: f64,
#   ) -> SpectralCoordinate<N_PRIME>
#
# where the target coordinate space (N') is determined by the reframe
# ceremony's target-domain parameter. Fractal::Lens carrier consumed as:
#
#   Fractal::Lens {
#       ref_: sc_in.oid(),         // origin coordinate identity
#       data: basis_shift.serialize(),
#       target: sc_out.oid(),      // target coordinate identity
#   }
#
# The Lens's edge-not-containment IS structurally COORD's jump (references
# target by OID rather than containing it — the compressed state-space is
# addressable but not nested).

# === The primitive: jump ===
#
# COORD's jump-behavior at stability-domain boundary. Per Foerster A3,
# `Op(COORDi) = COORDi` holds within the stable domain; boundary crossing
# triggers `COORDi → COORDj` where j is determined by the reframe
# ceremony's target winding class on @torus.
#
# Semantics:
#   pre-condition: peer's `@pain` gradient (via @cyberpunk/algedonic.
#     sample_pain) exceeds threshold ε_pain within @cyberpunk/reframe.
#   post-condition: peer's coordinate has been re-projected to the target
#     winding class; @heterarchy_preserved holds (per below); the reframe
#     ceremony may materialize the jump via commit_as_fold (Seam §4 #8
#     ratify-with-qualification: materialize at @cyberpunk/reframe
#     altitude, not @knife's, to avoid DAG pollution).
#
# Failure modes:
#   - Target domain undecidable (@∂M crossing per Braverman-Yampolsky 2007);
#     default to @kintsugi/consent.pause(Φ) as external witness per
#     Seam §5 missed-item #2
#   - Cross-peer coordination: @knife emits content_oid (not naked_oid)
#     so that N peers can verify they're at the same coordinate; per
#     Seam §5 missed-item #3 (Rung 4 @dance discipline)

action jump(coord_in: @fractal.spectral_coordinate.SC, pain_delta: f64)
  -> @fractal.spectral_coordinate.SC {
  # State-space compression during @cyberpunk/reframe level-shift.
  # Substrate-decl only; Rust runtime lands at bootstrap/src/converge.rs.
}

# === The fixed-point check ===
#
# Foerster A3 `Op(COORDi) = COORDi` written as a bilateral predicate.
# Peer within stability domain i observes their own coordinate; the
# operator applied to that coordinate returns the same coordinate.
#
# Composes with @eigenform.is_fixed_point (LANDED per Taut §1):
#   is_fixed_point(coord, Op) ≡ stable_within(coord, domain_of(coord))

action stable_within(coord: @fractal.spectral_coordinate.SC, domain: @torus.winding_class)
  -> @glass.verdict {
  # Verdict: pass = coord is fixed-point within domain (@knife.jump not
  #   needed); partial(confidence) = near boundary (peer's @pain gradient
  #   is elevated but below ε_pain); failure(reason) = coord has exceeded
  #   domain boundary (@cyberpunk/reframe should fire).
  # Substrate-decl only; Rust runtime composes @cyberpunk/algedonic.
  #   sample_pain when landed (Reed Landing 8+9.6a forward-promise).
}

# === The heterarchy preservation property ===
#
# Per Seam `e8508f5` §5 missed-item #1 REFORMULATION:
#   Original spec `heterarchy_preserved(sc_before, sc_after)` was
#   TAUTOLOGICAL — SC<5>=SC<5> is compile-time-guaranteed.
#   Substrate-honest form: check that BOTH coordinates belong to the
#   same interior component of the Mandelbrot manifold (M∘), OR that
#   BOTH exceed to the boundary (∂M).
#
# Per Seam §4 #7 (stability-domain ruling):
#   M∘-vs-∂M decision at runtime is Turing-undecidable per Braverman-
#   Yampolsky 2007. bootstrap/src/gap.rs does NOT provide this primitive
#   (Mara `c753d5b` §10.2 provisional REJECTED). Default: emit
#   @kintsugi/consent.pause(Φ) as external witness; agent-in-transcript
#   (Alex or Pack) provides the boundary judgment.

property heterarchy_preserved(before: @fractal.spectral_coordinate.SC,
                              after: @fractal.spectral_coordinate.SC)
  -> @glass.verdict {
  # Bilateral predicate: M∘-membership preservation (or joint ∂M-crossing).
  # Turing-undecidable in general; default: @kintsugi/consent.pause(Φ)
  # emission for external witness (Seam §5 missed-item #2).
  #
  # At @knife.jump events, the standard verdict-composition four-way
  # (compile_settled ∧ loss_decreased ∧ identity_preserved ∧
  # admissibility_singleton) EXPECTS loss_decreased and identity_preserved
  # to fail (topology shifts; the coordinate transition is the design
  # target). heterarchy_preserved IS the load-bearing gate under jump
  # semantics — as long as M∘-membership is preserved (or joint ∂M-
  # crossing witnessed via consent.pause), the jump is admissible.
}

